    <p class="A-PAR16R-RW-ALL">Step 4: Select 'Continue' and proceed to verify your identity with your HKID or passport.</p>
<p class="A-PAR16R-RW-ALL"><strong>Tips:</strong></p>
<ul class="A-LSTU-RW-ALL">
 <li>Supported HKID type: New Smart HKID (2018 version)</li>
 <li>Supported passports: Australia, Belgium, Canada, India, Ireland, Italy, Jersey, Mexico, Philippines, Singapore, South Africa, United Kingdom, United States, Vietnam and Taiwan</li>
 <li>Not holding an eligible HKID or passport?<br> You can remove the HSBC HK App from your device through HSBC Online Banking. Simply log on to HSBC Online Banking and go to 'Banking' &gt; 'Security Settings' &gt; 'Manage your Security Device' &gt; 'Remove Device' to remove the HSBC HK App from your old device. You can then download and log on to the HSBC HK App on your new device and set up your Mobile Banking PIN (<a href="#manage-device" target="_self">Step-by-step guide for Manage device</a>).</li>
</ul>
</div></div>

        
    


